Subject: [PATCH 5/9] SecurityPkg/SecureBootConfigDxe: Take pop-ups and state
 from HII

The pop-ups of the Secure Boot configuration, from the confirmation to
delete PK to the reasons a key cannot be enrolled, are literals in the
code, and so is the Enabled/Disabled shown for the current state. The
latter is also set with HiiSetString() and no language, which writes the
same English word into every language the package has.

Move the pop-up text into the string package and show it through a small
helper, and set the state from two new strings one language at a time.

Signed-off-by: Eric Wu <eric3u@outlook.com>
---
 .../SecureBootConfigImpl.c                    | 241 ++++++++++++------
 .../SecureBootConfigStrings.uni               |  21 ++
 2 files changed, 185 insertions(+), 77 deletions(-)

